{
  "note": "THE PIN for the TailscaleKit.xcframework the iPhone app embeds (Phase 316.3). build/build-tailscalekit.mjs is its reader, and the Xcode phase 'TailscaleKit is vendored' reads its commit. TailscaleKit is BUILT from this commit's source with Go and Xcode, never downloaded as a binary, so the gate is on the SOURCE archive: its sha256 was recorded on the first fetch and is checked on every fetch after it, and its pax header must name the commit. To move the pin, change commit, source.url and goModGo together, set source.sha256, modules and buildList to null in the same commit, and run node build/build-tailscalekit.mjs --record once; it fills only null fields. privacy.categories is his decision (build/p316/SPEC.md §6 decision 8), and the build refuses when the built binary needs a category that is not here, or no longer needs one that is. modules is every Go module compiled into the device slice, with the licence its own licence file reads; licence acknowledgements ship with the first phase that distributes to anyone but him (SPEC §7). buildList is `go list -m all` without its first line, stored sorted by JavaScript code unit and compared as a SET, so a byte diff against Go's own order shows a drift that is not one (Go's order differs from Masterminds/semver on). THE BUILD MAKES ONE CHANGE TO THIS SOURCE (316.3's hardening round, his ruling of 2026-09-23 on the node's diagnostic logs, \"Turn them off\"): NO_LOGS_PATCH in build/build-tailscalekit.mjs adds the export tailscale_no_logs_no_support(), which sets tsnet's own TS_NO_LOGS_NO_SUPPORT switch for the process and answers whether tsnet now reads it, because an app cannot set that variable for itself; each edit is anchored on text the pinned source holds exactly once, and the patch is part of the stamp's digest. The cost: Tailscale's support cannot see this node's logs.",
